---
/**
 * A page's answer block: the few sentences that resolve the question the
 * standfirst poses, before the detail ladder begins. Part of the disclosure
 * pattern in docs/design/site-information-architecture.md.
 *
 * Keep it to three to five sentences, plain words, rounded figures, every
 * number attributed. Exact figures belong in the rungs below it, except on
 * accounting pages where the arithmetic itself is the subject.
 */
---

<div class="answer">
  <span class="answer__label" aria-hidden="true">In short</span>
  <div class="answer__body">
    <slot />
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  /* The shared accent-rule recipe: 3px rule + --inset-box, as .callout. No
     right padding, because there is no background or right border for it to
     inset from; it would only shorten the line for no visible reason. */
  .answer {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding: .2rem 0 .2rem var(--inset-box);
    margin-block: 1.4rem;
  }
  .answer__label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: .6rem; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: .13em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .answer__body { font-size: 1.02rem; }
  .answer__body :global(p:last-child) { margin-bottom: 0; }
</style>
